# Potts, letter X

Xavier.; Xavier.

@LJCont 65. I spoke with one who was said to be Xavier. (His lot.)

@DMin 4570. Francis Xavier, the second father of the Jesuits, appeared deep under the buttocks. He was a still more subtle magician (than Anthony), operating profanely through conjugial love and innocence... Perhaps it is another. @4603[end]. @LJPost 67.

Xenophon.; Xenophon.

@CL 156. [151a]. In and around (the Athens there) dwell the ancient wise ones of Greece, as Xenophon, etc.

Xiphoid.; Xiphoid.

@AC 9236. The inhabitants of the moon... relate to the scutiform or Xiphoid cartilage, to which the ribs are joined in front...

